  "details": "see: title.\n\nSTR:\n\n1. take a photo\n\n2. print it out\n\n3. start editing its caption/custom message\n\n4. ask someone to grab the print that you're editing\n\n5. submit the new caption\n\nwhat should've happened:\n\n6. the new caption gets saved and synchronized among everyone in the instance\n\nwhat happens:\n\n6. nothing\n\nLooks like the prints use a system akin to Udon's networking ownership, and when you grab a print you become its owner, so then the person submitting a new caption doesn't have the 'right' to request sync of the new value.\n\nPS: if the other person drops the print, and you grab it before clicking save/submit/however it's called, the new caption syncs just fine, probably because you're the networking owner of the print again.",
